::: {#29c1bad3 .cell execution_count=5}
``` {.python .cell-code}
def root_at(edges, n, root):
    """Parent array of an undirected tree. parent[root] = -1."""
    adj = [[] for _ in range(n)]
    for u, v in edges:
        adj[u].append(v)
        adj[v].append(u)
    parent = [-2] * n
    parent[root] = -1
    q = deque([root])
    while q:
        u = q.popleft()
        for v in adj[u]:
            if parent[v] == -2:
                parent[v] = u
                q.append(v)
    return parent


def sizes_and_heights(parent):
    n = len(parent)
    children = [[] for _ in range(n)]
    root = parent.index(-1)
    for v, p in enumerate(parent):
        if p >= 0:
            children[p].append(v)
    order = []
    q = deque([root])
    while q:
        u = q.popleft()
        order.append(u)
        for c in children[u]:
            q.append(c)
    sz = [1] * n
    height = [0] * n
    for u in reversed(order):
        for c in children[u]:
            sz[u] += sz[c]
            height[u] = max(height[u], height[c] + 1)
    return sz, height


par = root_at(R_EDGES, 10, 0)
assert par == [-1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 2, 4, 4, 6]
sz, ht = sizes_and_heights(par)
assert sz == [10, 5, 3, 1, 3, 1, 2, 1, 1, 1]
assert ht == [3, 2, 2, 0, 1, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0]
assert root_at(R_EDGES, 10, 4) == [1, 4, 0, 0, -1, 1, 2, 4, 4, 6]
assert sizes_and_heights(root_at(R_EDGES, 10, 4))[1][4] == 5
```
:::


### Four shapes

| Name | Rule | Count, when it applies |
|---|---|---|
| Full | every node has $0$ or $2$ children | $n_0 = n_2 + 1$ leaves and binary nodes |
| Complete | every level is full except possibly the last, which is packed on the left | height $\lfloor \log_2 n \rfloor$ |
| Perfect | full, and every leaf has the same depth | $2^{h+1} - 1$ nodes at edge-height $h$ |
| Balanced | at every node the two subtree edge-heights differ by at most $1$ | height $O(\log n)$ |

Perfect implies complete, and perfect implies full. Complete implies balanced. Nothing else is true.

