::: {.callout-note collapse="true" title="[E] Balanced binary tree"}
[LC 110 · Balanced Binary Tree](https://leetcode.com/problems/balanced-binary-tree/){difficulty="Easy"}. Return the edge-height, or a failure mark when a side already failed or the two heights differ by more than $1$. A single node is balanced. The left spine `[1,2,null,3]` is not: the root's sides differ by $2$.

::: {#6b589755 .cell execution_count=86}
``` {.python .cell-code}
def is_balanced(root):
    def height(node):
        if node is None:
            return -1
        left, right = height(node.left), height(node.right)
        if left is None or right is None or abs(left - right) > 1:
            return None
        return 1 + max(left, right)
    return height(root) is not None

assert is_balanced(Node(1))
assert not is_balanced(from_level([1, 2, None, 3]))
```
