::: {.callout-note collapse="true" title="[E] Symmetric tree"}
[LC 101 · Symmetric Tree](https://leetcode.com/problems/symmetric-tree/){difficulty="Easy"}. Compare the tree with itself and cross the children. `[1,2,2,3,4,4,3]` is symmetric. `[1,2,2,null,3,null,3]` is not: both $3$s are right children.

::: {#baeed316 .cell execution_count=87}
``` {.python .cell-code}
def is_symmetric(root):
    def mirror(a, b):
        if a is None or b is None:
            return a is b
        return a.val == b.val and mirror(a.left, b.right) and mirror(a.right, b.left)
    return mirror(root, root)

assert is_symmetric(from_level([1, 2, 2, 3, 4, 4, 3]))
assert not is_symmetric(from_level([1, 2, 2, None, 3, None, 3]))
```
