::: {.callout-note collapse="true" title="[E] Leaf-similar trees"}
[LC 872 · Leaf-Similar Trees](https://leetcode.com/problems/leaf-similar-trees/){difficulty="Easy"}. The shape does not matter: collect each tree's leaves from left to right. `[1,2,3]` and `[1,3,2]` give $2, 3$ and $3, 2$.

::: {#4fcbb577 .cell execution_count=88}
``` {.python .cell-code}
def leaf_similar(a, b):
    def leaves(node, out):
        if node is None:
            return
        if node.left is None and node.right is None:
            out.append(node.val)
            return
        leaves(node.left, out)
        leaves(node.right, out)
    left, right = [], []
    leaves(a, left)
    leaves(b, right)
    return left == right

assert not leaf_similar(from_level([1, 2, 3]), from_level([1, 3, 2]))
assert leaf_similar(from_level([1, 2, 3]), from_level([1, 2, 3]))
```
