::: {.callout-note collapse="true" title="[E] Sum of root-to-leaf numbers"}
[LC 129 · Sum Root to Leaf Numbers](https://leetcode.com/problems/sum-root-to-leaf-numbers/){difficulty="Medium"}. The number so far is the state passed down, and a leaf adds it. `[1,2,3]` is $12 + 13 = 25$.

::: {#faf263f5 .cell execution_count=89}
``` {.python .cell-code}
def sum_numbers(root):
    def walk(node, so_far):
        if node is None:
            return 0
        so_far = so_far * 10 + node.val
        if node.left is None and node.right is None:
            return so_far
        return walk(node.left, so_far) + walk(node.right, so_far)
    return walk(root, 0)

assert sum_numbers(from_level([1, 2, 3])) == 25
```
