::: {.callout-note collapse="true" title="[E] Path sum II"}
[LC 113 · Path Sum II](https://leetcode.com/problems/path-sum-ii/){difficulty="Medium"}. Carry the remaining target and one shared path, and copy the path only at a leaf that hits zero. On `[5,4,8,11,null,13,4,7,2,null,null,5,1]` with target $22$ the paths are $[5,4,11,2]$ and $[5,8,4,5]$.

::: {#fc60beb3 .cell execution_count=90}
``` {.python .cell-code}
def path_sum_ii(root, target):
    out, path = [], []

    def walk(node, rest):
        if node is None:
            return
        path.append(node.val)
        rest -= node.val
        if node.left is None and node.right is None and rest == 0:
            out.append(path[:])
        walk(node.left, rest)
        walk(node.right, rest)
        path.pop()

    walk(root, target)
    return out

sample = from_level([5, 4, 8, 11, None, 13, 4, 7, 2, None, None, 5, 1])
assert path_sum_ii(sample, 22) == [[5, 4, 11, 2], [5, 8, 4, 5]]
```
