::: {.callout-note collapse="true" title="[E] Subordinates"}
[CSES 1674 · Subordinates](https://cses.fi/problemset/task/1674). A boss may have a larger label, so the order is a BFS, and the reverse of that order adds each employee's subordinates plus one into the boss. Bosses `1 1 2 3` ($n = 5$) print `4 1 1 0 0`.

::: {#2a57729a .cell execution_count=91}
``` {.python .cell-code}
def subordinates(bosses):
    n = len(bosses) + 1
    children = [[] for _ in range(n + 1)]
    for i, boss in enumerate(bosses, start=2):
        children[boss].append(i)
    order = [1]
    head = 0
    while head < len(order):
        order.extend(children[order[head]])
        head += 1
    sub = [0] * (n + 1)
    for v in reversed(order):
        if v != 1:
            sub[bosses[v - 2]] += sub[v] + 1
    return sub[1:]

assert subordinates([1, 1, 2, 3]) == [4, 1, 1, 0, 0]
```
