::: {.callout-note collapse="true" title="[M] Not assigning edge weights"}
[CF 1627C · Not Assigning](https://codeforces.com/problemset/problem/1627/C){rating="1400"}. A vertex of degree $3$ or more is impossible, and a path is weighted $2, 3, 2, 3, \ldots$ from either leaf. The path $1-2-3-4$ gets `[2, 3, 2]`. The star on four vertices gets `-1`.

::: {#412ad382 .cell execution_count=93}
``` {.python .cell-code}
def not_assigning(n, edges):
    adj = [[] for _ in range(n + 1)]
    for i, (u, v) in enumerate(edges):
        adj[u].append((v, i))
        adj[v].append((u, i))
    start = 0
    for v in range(1, n + 1):
        if len(adj[v]) >= 3:
            return -1
        if len(adj[v]) == 1:
            start = v
    weight = [0] * (n - 1)
    prev, cur, w = 0, start, 2
    for _ in range(n - 1):
        for nxt, i in adj[cur]:
            if nxt != prev:
                weight[i] = w
                w = 5 - w
                prev, cur = cur, nxt
                break
    return weight

assert not_assigning(4, [(1, 2), (2, 3), (3, 4)]) == [2, 3, 2]
assert not_assigning(4, [(1, 2), (1, 3), (1, 4)]) == -1
```
:::


