::: {.callout-note collapse="true" title="[M] Colour the edges at each vertex differently"}
[AC abc146_d · Coloring Edges on Tree](https://atcoder.jp/contests/abc146/tasks/abc146_d). $\Delta$ colours are enough: root at $1$ and give each child edge the next colour, skipping the parent edge's colour. The star with edges $1-2$, $1-3$, $1-4$ needs $3$ colours, and they come out `1 2 3` in input order.

::: {#a4a73da3 .cell execution_count=94}
``` {.python .cell-code}
def colour_edges(n, edges):
    adj = [[] for _ in range(n + 1)]
    for i, (a, b) in enumerate(edges):
        adj[a].append((b, i))
        adj[b].append((a, i))
    delta = max(len(adj[v]) for v in range(1, n + 1))
    colour = [0] * (n - 1)
    parent_colour = [0] * (n + 1)
    seen = [False] * (n + 1)
    seen[1] = True
    order = [1]
    head = 0
    while head < len(order):
        u = order[head]
        head += 1
        c = 1
        for v, i in adj[u]:
            if seen[v]:
                continue
            if c == parent_colour[u]:
                c += 1
            colour[i] = c
            parent_colour[v] = c
            c += 1
            seen[v] = True
            order.append(v)
    return delta, colour

assert colour_edges(4, [(1, 2), (1, 3), (1, 4)]) == (3, [1, 2, 3])
```
:::


