::: {.callout-note collapse="true" title="[M] How many scans draw the tree"}
[CF 1830A · Copil Copac Draws Trees](https://codeforces.com/problemset/problem/1830/A){rating="1400"}. Root at $1$, and a vertex waits for the next scan exactly when its parent edge has a smaller input index than its parent's. Edges given as $2-3$ then $1-2$ take $2$ scans: $3$ is queued before the edge that draws $2$.

::: {#b8e4ad89 .cell execution_count=96}
``` {.python .cell-code}
def scan_count(n, edges):
    adj = [[] for _ in range(n + 1)]
    for i, (u, v) in enumerate(edges):
        adj[u].append((v, i))
        adj[v].append((u, i))
    idx = [-1] * (n + 1)
    scans = [0] * (n + 1)
    seen = [False] * (n + 1)
    seen[1] = True
    scans[1] = 1
    order = [1]
    best = 1
    head = 0
    while head < len(order):
        u = order[head]
        head += 1
        for v, i in adj[u]:
            if seen[v]:
                continue
            seen[v] = True
            idx[v] = i
            scans[v] = scans[u] + (idx[v] < idx[u])
            best = max(best, scans[v])
            order.append(v)
    return best

assert scan_count(3, [(2, 3), (1, 2)]) == 2
```
:::


